From f214b7f478a036fa7cf79f42be23c74514a13df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:15:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: nfc: nxp,nci: describe an optional
 reference clock

Carry the reviewed change into the maintained LTS tree. Preserve the
original author, timestamp, source notices and assistance disclosures.
Keep the existing LTS allocation, I2C ID and NCI interfaces. The
optional clock reconciliation omits newer-base cleanup already absent
from LTS.

The actual NCI close/reset/receive/removal model reproduces nine wrong
baseline cases and none of ten after repair. Nine optional-clock/probe
cases and nine teardown/clock regression variants pass their
contracts. WCNSS selection/classification is already present and
tested separately. Sixty ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT native objects
compile without diagnostics using nonpermissive CFI, including
built-in/module and ACPI-off/on paths. All nineteen family DTBs pass
the full schema; sixteen remain identical, and the three Madai
variants gain only NFC and its bus/pin configuration. Seventy-five
inherited DTC warnings are retained without a new diagnostic.

Core services, locks, IRQ completion, bus, clocks and scheduling are
modeled. Physical NFC/radio, concurrent firmware, complete driver core
and final-image qualification remain open. Codex prepared the LTS port
and qualification. Human DCO and owner/security review remain pending;
no sign-off, phone action, Wi-Fi scan or publication is claimed.

Original reviewed changelog and disclosures:

Describe one external reference clock named ref. Require clocks and
clock-names together and retain existing clockless descriptions.

Port of Timothy Schmidt's original implementation bca73ac16d42. Author
and timestamp are preserved. The port, changelog and qualification
used OpenAI Codex assistance. Human review and DCO certification
remain pending. No agent Signed-off-by tag is added.

Backported from commit 46ebc8c8e500 ("dt-bindings: net: nfc: nxp,nci:
describe an optional reference clock")
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml          | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
index 364b361511808..b47ba2e589b2b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,13 @@ properties:
   enable-gpios:
     description: Output GPIO pin used for enabling/disabling the controller
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Optional external reference clock for the controller
+
+  clock-names:
+    const: ref
+
   firmware-gpios:
     description: Output GPIO pin used to enter firmware download mode
 
@@ -38,6 +45,10 @@ required:
   - interrupts
   - reg
 
+dependencies:
+  clocks: [clock-names]
+  clock-names: [clocks]
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
-- 
